# Verification gate scratch output (publishes, screenshots).
# Note this also catches MatrixDesktop/artifacts/, which is where ad-hoc publish experiments
# have landed; the gate itself only writes to the repo-root artifacts/gate/.
artifacts/

# Secrets. Nothing matching these has ever existed in this repo and none is expected to:
# it is a public repository that talks to no service and holds no credential. They are here
# as insurance, because the cost of the rule is nothing and the cost of one accidental
# `git add` of a local .env is a rotated key and a rewritten history.
.env
.env.*
*.env
secrets.json
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.local.json
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.snk
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
.npmrc
.netrc
# Second pass, 2026-09-11. id_ed25519 is the notable omission: it has been the default
# ssh-keygen type for years, so listing id_rsa without it covered the older case only.
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
_netrc
.git-credentials
credentials.json
service-account.json
.pypirc
.pgpass
*.keystore
*.jks
*.crt
*.cer
local.settings.json
*.publishsettings
appsettings.Production.json

# Deliberately NOT ignored, though a naive secrets sweep will suggest them:
#   nuget.config        a normal, committed .NET project file
#   appsettings.json    likewise; only the Development/Local/Production variants hold
#                       machine or environment specifics
# Ignoring either would hide a file that belongs in version control.
